  "description": "THE CROSS-LEVEL WITNESS, synthesized by botDriverV2 from three legs: level 0 (walk to (88,168), then exit through the teleporter at oel (0,128)), level 94 (walk to (216,200), then exit through (304,160)), level 0 (arrival, no targets). The CALLER names each teleporter; the driver never searches the graph. Unlike transition-west-return, whose crossings come from a hand-authored hold, every tick here is planned around real geometry in BOTH levels — level 94 is walled by a TreeLarge pixelmask and nine cliffsides, so the return route has to be planned, not guessed. It also pins the seam the physics refuses: the aim point for an exit is the trigger's centre, which for level 0's west pair at (0,128)/(0,144) means y=136 and not the ambiguous band y in (141,146) where both volumes overlap with different arrivals. Two transitions, at the ticks the transitions records name.",
